Z||000000||beachbomb||08-09-2001||02:27 PM||||Hey all, quick question, anybody know anything about a 4 cyclinder 1983 Camaro? A friend of mine just bought one, supposedly the four cyclinder was only sold in canada and was limited to 5,000 total made. Any help with this is greatly appreciated, thanks..jim(2 '84 Indys)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigzach_22.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||saleenfiero||08-09-2001||02:32 PM||||I'm thinking they only sold that many 4 banger camaros because a 4 cyl camaro is a contradiction.  I'm sure they were sold in the states too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||08-09-2001||02:34 PM||||From 1982 until 1984 or 1985 the F-body cars (Camaro and Firebird) base cars came standard with a 2.5L Iron Duke 4-cyl. It was not a "Canada Only" I am not sure how many F-body cars with 4-cyl were sold. I know most folks and dealers ordered the 2.8L V-6 option for the base cars. I know someone at work who bought an 1983 Firebird with a blown 4-cyl in it. He's installing a 1980 Pontiac 301 V-8 in it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||08-09-2001||03:17 PM||||I've seen exactly *one* F-body (think it was an 82 Firebird) with a Duke, and a 4-speed. <BR>This was 10-15 years ago at a yard/estate sale, near Atlanta.<BR>People weren't exactly lining up to test drive it. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroKyle||08-09-2001||09:09 PM||||And I thought a Fiero was slow with the Iron Duke, lol. Now that would be funny. A Iron Duke Firebird pulls up to a Iron Duke Fiero and the Fiero blows its doors off infront of everyone. LOL||||reg||1
Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||08-09-2001||09:25 PM||||WOW!!<P>I never thought I would hear of anyone owning another one.<P>EXEXEXEXEX Girlfriend had one. it was an auto with air!!<P>Slowest car I have driven.<P>Whats really to know?? there not worth anything because of the rarity. The motor was basically identical to an s-10.<P>I wouldn't spin the tire on gravel...<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000006||baldlobo||08-10-2001||12:14 AM||||there's nothing wrong with an Iron Bird all you need is N2O or something else<BR>second or third write up on this page: <A HREF="http://www.0rdernet.com/Mean_Pontiac/82lot1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.0rdernet.com/Mean_Pontiac/82lot1.htm</A> <BR>And then there is one on here: <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/al/yousmellit/sweet.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/al/yousmellit/sweet.html</A> <P>[This message has been edited by baldlobo (edited 08-10-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by baldlobo (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||08-10-2001||01:52 AM||||I find this very hard to believe!<P>see this link and look for:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/al/yousmellit/sweet.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/al/yousmellit/sweet.html</A>  <P>'82 Camaro Sport Coupe, 4cyl. <BR>Bored and Stroked from 151ci- 210ci., twin 65mm. <BR>throttle bodies, B&M Shift kit w/ratchet shifter <BR>4spd auto with OD. other mods include: <BR>tach, oil pressure meter, and boost meter. <BR>Last but not least is the posi-traction 3.73 rear end. <BR>290-300hp and torque like you wont believe.<P>First a 151ci is 2.5L, a 210ci is 3.4L.<BR>Even the race built SD4 cannot get to 3.4L!<BR>The largest an SD4 can get is 3.2L. (Strokes to 3.0 and bored to 3.2L)<BR>I highly doubt a stock 2.5 can be bored and stroked that big. Second, Why does he need a boost gauge? He doesn't mention a turbo or SC.<BR>The 2.5L in the RWD cars/trucks had the same bottom end as the FWD engines. I find it very amazing that the bottom end can hold together at 200HP with only 2-bolt mains and he says he's at 290-300.<P>Maybe we should Email him for the exact specs, I'm sure an 84 SE Fiero would fly past many V-8 cars with a 300hp 4-cyl. <P><BR>||||reg||4
